<title>USA: Coca-Cola opens bottling plant in Ghana.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola opens bottling plant in Ghana.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Coca-Cola Co said on Thursday it opened a new bottling plant in Accra, Ghana.</p>
<p>The plant, one of the first of this type in West Africa, was owned by The Coca-Cola Bottling Co of Ghana, a joint venture between the Ghanaian government, Coca-Cola and the Africa Growth Fund, the company said.</p>
<p>The company would continue to produce Coca-Cola, Fanta, Sprite and Krest at the new production facility and existing plant in Kumasi, Ghana, it said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
